{
  "schemaVersion": "atm.workItem.v0.2",
  "workItemId": "ATM-GOV-0364",
  "title": "Remove the governance round-trip tax on a single task card",
  "status": "running",
  "milestone": null,
  "dependencies": [],
  "acceptance": [
    "ACC-1 A path added by `tasks scope add` is included in the governed delivery bundle for that task without any further command. Whether the bundle reads the direction lock or the ledger is an implementation choice; that the two agree is the contract.",
    "ACC-2 `tasks import --force` preserves an existing active claim and task status unless `--force-overwrite-claims` is passed. When it does displace a claim, it says so with the existing displacement event.",
    "ACC-3 One `taskflow pre-close` run enumerates every prerequisite that will block `close --write`, including repo-level validators and the runner kind they require, regardless of how many other blockers are currently present.",
    "ACC-4 Evidence recorded before a commit that does not change any file under test remains fresh after it. Evidence for a validator whose subject did change is still expired.",
    "ACC-5 `<command> <subcommand> --help` lists the flags that subcommand accepts. A flag belonging only to a sibling subcommand does not appear.",
    "ACC-6 A focused test measures the round trips required to land a minimal synthetic card and fails if that count regresses, so this tax cannot silently return.",
    "ACC-7 Each of the five tracked backlog items is set to Resolved with the commit that fixed it, and each names the focused test that will report the regression if it returns."
  ],
